//@version=6
// =============================================================================================
// NQ / MNQ — BOS/CHoCH.  v7
//
// ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │ BEFORE YOU READ THE RESULT — TradingView "Script execution" (the dropdown under the        │
// │ backtest report) must have ONLY  "On bar close"  ticked.                                   │
// │                                                                                            │
// │ Measured on a live MNQ 30m chart, same script, same period:                                │
// │      On bar close only ....  183 trades   +$9,380   PF 1.58   maxDD  2.59%                 │
// │      All four ticked .......  248 trades  −$16,247   PF 0.56   maxDD 16.61%                │
// │                                                                                            │
// │ This is not fragility. The rule is `close > pivot` — a break CONFIRMED at the bar's close. │
// │ "On order fill" / "history bar tick" / "realtime bar tick" re-run the script DURING the    │
// │ bar, so `close` becomes the running price and every intrabar poke through a pivot that     │
// │ reverses before the close fires a false BOS. Ticking those boxes does not make the test    │
// │ more realistic; it silently replaces this strategy with a worse one.                       │
// └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
//
// TIMEFRAME MATTERS MORE THAN ANY SETTING. Use 30m or 60m. On 5m this rule LOSES: my engine
// gives PF 0.96-0.99 there and coin-flip entries with the same stop beat it 65% of the time. On
// 1m and 2m it is significantly negative (t = −2.45, −2.68). A losing 5-minute backtest is not a
// bug, it is the documented result.
//
// FIX HISTORY — every one of these was a real defect, found by diffing this script against the
// Python engine the research was done on:
//   v7  commission now scales with the contract. The sizing note below says to trade MNQ (a 2×ATR
//       stop on NQ risks ~$2,000); the fee was hardcoded at $2.00/order, right for the E-mini and
//       10× too heavy on a Micro, where it ate ~5% of gross profit. Following both instructions
//       as written was self-defeating.
//   v6  THE ENTRY GATE (see grpT). A session-string window admitted the session's FIRST bar,
//       which the engine excludes. Worth 35 extra trades and −$8,318 on 30m. With it corrected
//       this script reproduces the engine exactly.
//   v6  volatility sizing defaulted ON while the reference figures are fixed-1-contract, so the
//       P&L could not match regardless of anything else. Now off, and under the spec lock.
//   v4  the run counter tested `bias` AFTER reassigning it, so it never reset on a structure
//       flip — silently turning "enter on the second BOS" into "enter on every BOS".
//   v2  the stop was measured from the SIGNAL bar's close but filled at the NEXT bar's open, so
//       every stop sat at the wrong distance. Now anchored to strategy.position_avg_price.
//
// DIAGNOSING A MISMATCH. Each statistic below identifies ONE input and is flat in the others.
// Net P&L is the worst diagnostic available — it moves with all of them at once.
//   win rate   -> stop multiple   2.0×ATR = 39-40%,  1.0 = 27-29%,  0.5 = 16-17%
//   trade count-> nBos            ~150-190 at 2,     ~290-400 at 1  (same window)
//   comm % of gross profit -> contract size   NQ 0.3-0.5%,  MNQ at $2.00/order 2.9-5.2%
// TradingView caches inputs PER CHART and a stale value survives a script update, which is what
// "LOCK the tested spec" exists for. Read the diagnostic label before believing any number.
// =============================================================================================

strategy("NQ BOS/CHoCH book", overlay = true, initial_capital = 100000,
     default_qty_type = strategy.fixed, default_qty_value = 1,
     commission_type = strategy.commission.cash_per_order,
     // Auto by contract size. Deliberately NOT an input: a hand-set fee is exactly the footgun
     // v7 exists to remove. Edit this line if your broker differs.
     commission_value = syminfo.pointvalue < 10 ? 0.50 : 2.00,
     slippage = 2, pyramiding = 0, calc_on_every_tick = false,
     process_orders_on_close = false)

// Same expression as the commission argument above, kept as a variable so the diagnostic label
// can report it. Pine has no runtime accessor for the configured commission.
commPerOrder = syminfo.pointvalue < 10 ? 0.50 : 2.00

// ── preset ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
preset = input.string("30m core", "Preset", options = ["30m core", "60m core", "custom"],
     tooltip = "30m core: range filter 1.0 ATR.  60m core: range filter off. " +
               "Run BOTH on separate charts — that is the tested book. They correlate 0.28.")

grpS = "Structure"
swingK  = input.int(3, "Swing confirmation bars (k)", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = grpS,
     tooltip = "A pivot needs k bars either side, so it is invisible until k bars later. " +
               "k had a DIFFERENT best value at every timeframe tested — it is the fragile axis. " +
               "Left at the neutral 3 deliberately.")
nBosIn  = input.int(2, "Enter on the Nth BOS", minval = 1, maxval = 5, group = grpS)
lockSpec= input.bool(true, "LOCK the tested spec (ignore cached chart settings)", group = grpS,
     tooltip = "TradingView remembers input values PER CHART. If this script was added before a " +
               "revision, your saved values persist and silently override the defaults. With this " +
               "on, nBos, the stop multiple and volatility sizing are forced to the tested values.")
nBos    = lockSpec ? 2 : nBosIn

grpF = "Filters"
useEma  = input.bool(true, "Require price on the trend side of the EMA", group = grpF)
emaLen  = input.int(200, "EMA length", minval = 10, group = grpF)
mdIn    = input.float(1.0, "Refuse entries within N x ATR of the EMA", minval = 0, step = 0.25, group = grpF)

grpR = "Risk"
atrLen  = input.int(14, "ATR length", minval = 2, group = grpR)
atrMultIn = input.float(2.0, "Stop = N x ATR", minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = grpR)
atrMult   = lockSpec ? 2.0 : atrMultIn
useChoch= input.bool(true, "Exit on the opposite BOS (CHoCH)", group = grpR)

grpV = "Volatility-targeted sizing"
useVTIn = input.bool(false, "Size inversely to recent volatility", group = grpV,
     tooltip = "OFF by default: the reference figures were measured at a FIXED 1 contract, so " +
               "turning this on makes the P&L incomparable to them. It is a separately validated " +
               "overlay — max drawdown 36.3% -> 10.5% while Sharpe ROSE 1.31 -> 1.60 — and it " +
               "changes size only, never direction, so trade count and win rate are unaffected.")
useVT   = lockSpec ? false : useVTIn
vtLook  = input.int(60, "Volatility lookback (bars)", minval = 10, group = grpV)
vtCap   = input.float(2.0, "Maximum size multiplier", minval = 1.0, step = 0.5, group = grpV)
baseQty = input.float(1.0, "Base contracts", minval = 0.1, step = 0.1, group = grpV)

grpT = "Session (exchange time)"
// THE ENTRY GATE. The engine admits an entry only when ALL THREE hold:
//     1. the signal bar is in session
//     2. the NEXT bar is also in session   -- the fill is at the next open, and an entry that
//        fills at 16:00 is filling after the cash close in thin liquidity
//     3. the signal bar is NOT the session's first bar
// Clock arithmetic on the bar's OPEN time in exchange timezone: exact, and no look-ahead, because
// the calendar is known in advance and the prices are not. At 30m this admits 10:00 to 15:00.
// Do NOT go back to an input.session() window — a session string cannot express condition 2,
// which is why the old formulation had to be replaced rather than patched.
sessStart = input.int(570, "Session start (minutes after midnight, exchange time)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "570 = 09:30. Change only to test a different session.")
sessEnd   = input.int(960, "Session end (minutes after midnight, exchange time)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "960 = 16:00.")
showSess  = input.bool(true, "Tint the entry window", group = grpT)
flatEOD   = input.bool(false, "Flatten at the session close (intraday-only variant)", group = grpT,
     tooltip = "OFF = the tested spec: a position is held until its stop or a CHoCH, which on 30m " +
               "means a 12.5h median hold and 35% of trades crossing the close. ON = forced flat " +
               "daily. On the full sample flattening looks cheap ($47,997 / PF 1.29 / 44.4% win " +
               "vs $63,165 / PF 1.38 / 39.0%), but split on the research/locked boundary the " +
               "ranking FLIPS: research favours flattening (Sharpe 1.96 vs 1.68), the LOCKED " +
               "third favours holding decisively ($32,642 / Sharpe 1.87 vs $15,182 / 0.95). " +
               "Turn it on for RISK reasons only — no overnight gap exposure, day-trade margin, " +
               "a prop-firm flat-by-close rule — and expect it to cost about HALF the P&L and " +
               "half the Sharpe. It is not an improvement.")

showDiag = input.bool(true, "Show diagnostics (settings actually in force)", group = "Diagnostics",
     tooltip = "On by default. The label on the last bar reports the values IN FORCE, which is " +
               "the only way to catch a cached input silently overriding a default.")

minDist = preset == "30m core" ? 1.0 : preset == "60m core" ? 0.0 : mdIn

// ── indicators ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
emaV = ta.ema(close, emaLen)
atrV = ta.atr(atrLen)

// Confirmed fractal pivots. ta.pivothigh(k,k) returns the pivot k bars back, so reading it on the
// current bar is causal: the value does not exist until the right-hand bars have printed.
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, swingK, swingK)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  swingK, swingK)
var float lastPH = na
var float lastPL = na
if not na(ph)
    lastPH := ph
if not na(pl)
    lastPL := pl

// ── structure ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var float brokeHi = na
var float brokeLo = na
var int   bias    = 0
var int   runLen  = 0

// `close` beyond the pivot, not `high`/`low` touching it. The confirmation is load-bearing: on my
// engine, switching to an intrabar touch costs PF 1.49 -> 1.20. See the execution-mode box above.
bosUp = not na(lastPH) and close > lastPH and (na(brokeHi) or lastPH != brokeHi)
bosDn = not na(lastPL) and close < lastPL and (na(brokeLo) or lastPL != brokeLo)
if bosUp
    brokeHi := lastPH
if bosDn
    brokeLo := lastPL
// The counter must be tested against the OLD bias and only then reassigned. Writing `bias := 1`
// first makes the following test trivially true, so the counter never resets on a structure flip.
if bosUp
    if bias == 1
        runLen := runLen + 1
    else
        bias   := 1
        runLen := 1
if bosDn
    if bias == -1
        runLen := runLen + 1
    else
        bias   := -1
        runLen := 1

// ── session gate ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tfMin    = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period) / 60
barMin   = hour * 60 + minute                          // bar OPEN, exchange timezone
inSess   = barMin >= sessStart and barMin < sessEnd
nextIn   = barMin + tfMin >= sessStart and barMin + tfMin < sessEnd
newSess  = inSess and not inSess[1]
canEnter = inSess and nextIn and not newSess

// ── filters ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
farEnough = minDist <= 0 or (not na(emaV) and not na(atrV) and math.abs(close - emaV) >= minDist * atrV)
okLong  = (not useEma or close > emaV) and farEnough
okShort = (not useEma or close < emaV) and farEnough
ready   = not na(atrV) and atrV > 0 and not na(emaV)

longSig  = bosUp and runLen >= nBos and okLong  and canEnter and ready
shortSig = bosDn and runLen >= nBos and okShort and canEnter and ready

// ── volatility-targeted size: bigger when quiet, smaller when wild. Causal. ──────────────────
avgAtr = ta.sma(atrV, vtLook)
vtMult = useVT and not na(avgAtr) and atrV > 0 ? math.min(avgAtr / atrV, vtCap) : 1.0
qty    = math.max(math.round(baseQty * vtMult), 1)

// ── orders ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The stop is anchored to the ACTUAL fill (strategy.position_avg_price), not to the signal bar's
// close. The ATR used is the one that was current when the signal fired.
var float atrAtSignal = na
var float stopLevel   = na

if (longSig or shortSig) and strategy.position_size == 0
    atrAtSignal := atrV

if longSig and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = qty)
if shortSig and strategy.position_size == 0
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = qty)

if strategy.position_size > 0 and na(stopLevel)
    stopLevel := strategy.position_avg_price - atrMult * atrAtSignal
if strategy.position_size < 0 and na(stopLevel)
    stopLevel := strategy.position_avg_price + atrMult * atrAtSignal
if strategy.position_size == 0
    stopLevel := na

if strategy.position_size > 0 and not na(stopLevel)
    strategy.exit("Lx", "L", stop = stopLevel)
if strategy.position_size < 0 and not na(stopLevel)
    strategy.exit("Sx", "S", stop = stopLevel)

// Track why positions close, so a win-rate mismatch can be attributed rather than guessed at.
var int nCloses = 0
var int nChoch  = 0
wasIn = strategy.position_size[1] != 0
if wasIn and strategy.position_size == 0
    nCloses += 1

if flatEOD and strategy.position_size != 0 and not inSess
    strategy.close_all(comment = "EOD flat")

if useChoch
    if strategy.position_size > 0 and bosDn
        strategy.close("L", comment = "CHoCH")
        nChoch += 1
    if strategy.position_size < 0 and bosUp
        strategy.close("S", comment = "CHoCH")
        nChoch += 1

if showDiag and barstate.islast
    var label lbl = na
    label.delete(lbl)
    lbl := label.new(bar_index, high,
         "symbol " + syminfo.ticker + "   tf " + timeframe.period +
         "\n$ per point " + str.tostring(syminfo.pointvalue) + "  (NQ 20 / MNQ 2)" +
         "\ncommission $" + str.tostring(commPerOrder) + "/order  (auto)" +
         "\n— gates in force —" +
         "\nnBos " + str.tostring(nBos) + "    stop " + str.tostring(atrMult) + " x ATR" +
         "\nrange filter " + str.tostring(minDist) + " x ATR" +
         "\nentry window " + str.tostring(math.round(sessStart + tfMin)) + "-" +
             str.tostring(math.round(sessEnd - tfMin)) + " (exchange minutes)" +
         "\nvol sizing " + (useVT ? "ON — P&L will not match reference" : "off") +
         "\n— exits —" +
         "\nposition closes " + str.tostring(nCloses) +
         "\n  of which CHoCH " + str.tostring(nChoch) +
         "\n  of which stops " + str.tostring(nCloses - nChoch) +
         "\n\nIf win rate is near 27%, the stop is running 1xATR, not 2." +
         "\nIf trades are near 290, nBos is running 1, not 2." +
         "\nIf either looks wrong, Script execution must be ON BAR CLOSE ONLY.",
         style = label.style_label_left, color = color.new(color.black, 15), textcolor = color.white)

// ── plots ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(emaV, "EMA 200", color.new(color.orange, 0), 2)
bU = plot(minDist > 0 ? emaV + minDist * atrV : na, "no-trade band", color.new(color.gray, 70))
bL = plot(minDist > 0 ? emaV - minDist * atrV : na, "no-trade band", color.new(color.gray, 70))
fill(bU, bL, color.new(color.gray, 92), title = "range — no entries here")
plot(stopLevel, "stop", color.new(color.red, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plotshape(bosUp and inSess, "BOS up",   shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color.new(color.teal, 0),   size = size.tiny)
plotshape(bosDn and inSess, "BOS down", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.maroon, 0), size = size.tiny)
bgcolor(showSess and canEnter ? color.new(color.blue, 94) : na, title = "entry window")

// =============================================================================================
// WHAT THESE RULES PRODUCED — docs/ib/STUDY_BOS_CHOCH.md, STUDY_LOWER_DD.md, STUDY_MNQ_LIVE.md
//
// NQ, Dec 2022 – Dec 2025, 1 contract, no volatility sizing:
//   30m leg (filter 1.0)   147 trades   +$71,483   PF 1.54   Sharpe 1.00   maxDD 15.6%   t 1.88
//   60m leg (filter 0)      43 trades   +$63,233   PF 2.37   Sharpe 1.08   maxDD 13.1%
//   LOCKED final third (268 sessions, never used to choose anything):
//                            30m +$47,072 Sharpe 1.39   |   60m +$28,065 Sharpe 1.07
//
// MNQ at $0.50/order, same window — and note the LOCKED block beats the research block, which is
// rare and is the strongest single thing that can be said for this rule:
//   full sample   147 trades  +$7,060  PF 1.53  40.1% win  maxDD $2,074  Sharpe 2.28
//   research 65%   91 trades  +$2,387  PF 1.34               maxDD $1,245  Sharpe 1.64
//   LOCKED   35%   56 trades  +$4,674  PF 1.75               maxDD $2,074  Sharpe 3.07
//
// Monte Carlo, 5,000 stationary-block-bootstrap paths on daily P&L:
//   net $   p5 1,232   median 6,969   p95 13,214        P(net < 0) = 2.3%
//   maxDD   p5 1,337   median 2,180   p95  3,922        P(DD > 2x realised) = 3.4%
//
// WHAT FAILS, so you do not rediscover it:
//   • 1m and 2m are SIGNIFICANTLY NEGATIVE (t = −2.45, −2.68). This does not scalp.
//   • At 5m, coin-flip entries with the same risk management beat it 65% of the time.
//   • Adding a 15m leg RAISED book drawdown to 37% for a Calmar of 0.26. Two legs, not three.
//   • An equity-curve brake (cut size after an 8% drawdown) made everything worse.
//   • SIX pre-specified variants — confirmation buffers, breakeven stops, time-of-day windows —
//     were tested with a locked holdout. NONE beat the baseline on both blocks. The rank
//     correlation between research and locked Sharpe was −0.429: the variant that looked WORST
//     in research was the BEST out of sample. Walk-forward re-selection cost −$3,857 against
//     never changing anything. Do not tune this. Tuning it is the documented way to lose money.
//   • PBO is 0.571 and t = 1.88 against a ~2.7 multiple-testing hurdle. The strategy is
//     profitable and out-of-sample positive; it is NOT a statistically established edge.
//   • There is NO ES DATA behind any of this. One instrument, one bull market, three years.
//
// SIZE: a 2×ATR stop on 30m NQ risks ~$2,000 per contract; on MNQ ~$200. The commission above
// scales with the contract automatically, so the two decisions no longer fight each other.
//
// Research tooling for education and analysis. Not financial advice.
// =============================================================================================
